# B306 application Kconfig.
#
# WHY AN APPLICATION Kconfig EXISTS AT ALL
# ----------------------------------------
# ~/ncs/v2.8.0 is a SHARED SDK install, compiled by every project that builds
# against it -- the Fusion Master DK image included. v45 patches five SDK files,
# and section 14 requires that "unrelated SDK consumers must still compile with
# instrumentation neutralized (guard everything behind a dedicated Kconfig,
# default n, selected only by the B306 app)".
#
# An application Kconfig is exactly that mechanism: symbols defined here land in
# autoconf.h, which every compiled file in the build sees -- including the
# patched SDK ones. A project that does not define BSF_V45_TRACE gets the
# neutralised macros and byte-identical object code.
#
# The patched files additionally test __has_include(<bsf_v45_trace.h>), which
# only this application puts on the global include path. Belt and braces: either
# condition failing disables the instrumentation completely.

menu "BioSpur Fusion B306"

config BSF_V45_TRACE
	bool "v45 four-channel BT trace instrumentation"
	default n
	help
	  Enables the BSF_V45_* markers in the patched NCS Bluetooth host and
	  SoftDevice Controller HCI driver, the four single-writer trace
	  channels, the dual-watermark wedge detector and the v45 corpse.

	  Leave this off for every project other than the B306 application.
	  With it off, every marker collapses to ((void)0) and the patched SDK
	  files produce the same object code as the pristine ones.

config BSF_V45_FAULT_INJECT
	bool "v45 fault-injection hooks (VALIDATION BUILDS ONLY)"
	default n
	depends on BSF_V45_TRACE
	help
	  Compiles in the V45 LEAK / V45 LEAK OFF vendor commands, which take
	  and release the singleton sync_evt_pool buffer.

	  This deliberately induces the suspected failure. It must never be
	  enabled in a fleet image. Stage B uses it on a single canary board to
	  prove the starvation -> phenotype consequence chain; that is a
	  different claim from "real wedges begin this way", and the run brief
	  must not conflate them.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
